      "reasons": {
        "CG01": "The source gives 30% as an assumed input for one simulated nature park. It is not a measured rate, and the claim stretches it to all municipal street-dog populations in Taiwan.",
        "CG02": "The source says the confidence intervals overlap a lot and the 2022–2024 change is statistically non-significant. That is the opposite of a significant reduction.",
        "CG03": "The source says the pyrometallurgical (-$13.95M/yr) and hydrometallurgical (-$10.69M/yr) routes lose money under these conditions. Only direct regeneration makes a profit.",
        "CG04": "Both sources come from the same internal runner at the same commit, so they are one result exported twice, not two independent replications. The run also failed 4 broader probes, which rules out complete readiness.",
        "CG05": "The source is a synthetic test of a threshold filter, and it found a NaN bug. It has no mortality data, so the claimed 40% reduction in deaths is unsupported.",
        "CG06": "The study is cross-sectional and found only a link with poor concentration, with no significant respiratory associations. It did not test the device or look at hospitalizations, so a causal claim is unsupported.",
        "CG07": "This is an open question. The source says the net result depends on local transport, cold-chain, spoilage and substitution figures, and none of them have been measured in the pilot.",
        "CG08": "The tender asks for a full service with staffing, billing audits and ISO 50001 certification. The repository is only a smart-meter protocol parser library, and nothing establishes buyer eligibility.",
        "CG09": "The claim matches the source: an observational estimate of 1,190 avoided deaths per year, with the ecological-confounding caveat and the 2010-exclusion sensitivity result both kept.",
        "CG10": "The probe at the pinned commit shows NaN readings appear in the ranked output because relative_water_level returns NaN rather than None. The 'unless sanitized upstream' wording does not go beyond the source."
      }
    },
