      "reasons": {
        "CG01": "The 30% immigration rate is a parameter in a Shoushan nature park simulation for a semi-closed reserve. The claim extends it to all Taiwanese municipal street-dog populations and calls it 'verified' and 'proven'.",
        "CG02": "The source says the 2022–2024 change is statistically non-significant and the confidence intervals overlap. The claim asserts a statistically significant reduction.",
        "CG03": "The source reports negative net profit for pyrometallurgical (-$13.95M/yr) and hydrometallurgical (-$10.69M/yr) routes. Only direct regeneration is positive. The claim states the opposite.",
        "CG04": "Both receipts come from the same internal commit and publisher, so there are not two independent replications. The commit also failed 4 broader probes, so 'complete production-ready privacy' is unsupported.",
        "CG05": "The source is a synthetic-data function probe that also found a NaN-handling defect. It has no mortality data, so the quantified 40% reduction in flood deaths is an unsupported leap.",
        "CG06": "The source is a cross-sectional study that found an association with lack of concentration and no significant respiratory associations. It cannot support a causal claim that a CO2 display reduces asthma hospitalizations.",
        "CG07": "The source says the transport distances, cold-chain energy, spoilage and substitution parameters have not been measured in the pilot. Whether the app achieves a net GHG reduction is therefore an open question.",
        "CG08": "The repository is a DLMS/COSEM protocol parser library. The tender needs on-site staffing, billing audit and ISO 50001 certification. Nothing supports calling the library a turnkey match or confirming buyer eligibility.",
        "CG09": "The claim matches the source: an observational pre/post estimate of 1,190 average annual avoided deaths, with ecological confounding noted and the result no longer significant when 2010 is excluded.",
        "CG10": "The pinned-commit probe receipt shows that a NaN latest_level passed to stations_highest_rel_level yields nan_in_ranked_stations=True, because relative_water_level returns NaN rather than None. The claim is scoped to that commit."
      }
    },
